<h2>Theatre and Folk Masks<wbr> from the New Forest</h2>
<p>False Faces is an artisanal mask studio making, training and performing with theatrical masks and puppets. Each piece is handcrafted in leather or wood, or produced using hybrid craft-and-digital techniques, designed as functional objects for the stage.</p>

<p>Every design is developed through rehearsal, workshop and performance, then refined in response. I work within the traditions of Lecoq pedagogy and Commedia dell'Arte theatre, as well as creating designs to meet the needs of specific productions.</p>

<p>My masks and puppets bring continental European traditions together with English heritage and folklore, drawing in particular on the history, landscape and culture of the New Forest and England's south coast.</p>

